  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "B"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>For&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn></math> possible values of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#8467;</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn></math>&nbsp;because values <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#8467;</mi></math>&nbsp;lie between <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>to</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></math>&nbsp;</p><p>We have to check values of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math>&nbsp;which lie between&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#8467;</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>to</mi><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#8467;</mi></math>.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#8467;</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#38;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#8467;</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn></math> can have&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></math> So possible subshells are <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn></math>.</p>"
  }
